\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A complex accretive weight}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{On a one-dimensional Hermitian space, the scalar operator
#{K=(1+i)I} in \ref{fdip-009K} has Hermitian part #{I/2}, so it
is strictly accretive. The paired value is #{Z_F=1+i}, and the
normalized bosonic factor is #{Z_B=(1+i)^{-1}}. Their product
is one. The density is not a positive probability density.}
